<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 April in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 April, from 630 to 1994.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/630">630 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,396 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Shahrbaraz usurps the Sasanian throne from Ardashir III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz">Shahrbaraz</a>, a leading Sasanian general under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-ii">Khosrow II</a> who had captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a> from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in 614, usurped the throne from Ardashir III. He was killed by Iranian nobles six weeks later, in the turmoil that preceded the Arab conquest.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shahrbaraz">Shahrbaraz</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1296">1296 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">730 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The English rout the Scots at the Battle of Dunbar</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An English army under John de Warenne, Earl of Surrey, routed the Scots near Dunbar in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-lothian">East Lothian</a> after Edward I's invasion and sack of Berwick. Scottish resistance collapsed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> Balliol surrendered and abdicated in July.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dunbar-1296">Battle of Dunbar</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-war-of-scottish-independence">First War of Scottish Independence</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-balliol">John Balliol</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1521">1521 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">505 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ferdinand Magellan is killed on Mactan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Magellan died fighting the forces of the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lapulapu">Lapulapu</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. Under Juan Sebastián Elcano, one ship of his fleet returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1522, completing the first circumnavigation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1650">1650 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">376 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Montrose's royalists are routed at Carbisdale</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Marquess of Montrose, landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> for the exiled Charles II, was defeated by Covenanter forces. He was captured and hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a> a month later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1791">1791 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">235 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Samuel Morse is born in Massachusetts</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Morse, painter turned inventor, was born in Charlestown. He developed an electric <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/telegraph">telegraph</a> and, with Alfred Vail, the code that bears his name.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1810">1810 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">216 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Beethoven dates the manuscript of Für Elise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Beethoven's autograph of the Bagatelle in A minor carried the date 27 April 1810. Unpublished in his lifetime, it appeared in 1867 and became one of the best-known piano pieces.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1945">1945 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Partisans capture Mussolini at Dongo</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Disguised in a German greatcoat in a convoy heading north, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a> was recognised and seized by Italian partisans near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-como">Lake Como</a>. He was shot the next day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benito-mussolini">Benito Mussolini</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1994">1994 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">32 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">South Africa holds its first all-race elections</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Millions of Black South Africans voted for the first time. The ANC won decisively and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a> became president, ending the apartheid order. The date is now Freedom Day.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
